listing:   run.sh (step qemu_capture)
toolchain: QEMU emulator version 8.2.2 (Debian 1:8.2.2+ds-0ubuntu1.18); TShark (Wireshark) 4.2.2 (Git v4.2.2 packaged as 4.2.2-1.1build3).
command:   qemu-system-x86_64 -machine q35 -nodefaults -display none -serial none -monitor none -no-reboot -boot order=n -netdev user,id=n0 -device e1000,netdev=n0,mac=52:54:00:12:34:56 -object filter-dump,id=f1,netdev=n0,file=net.pcap  (stopped after 20 s by timeout); then tshark -r net.pcap
date:      2026-10-09T19:16:47Z
machine:   Linux x86_64 (cloud build container)
exit code: 124
note:      exit code 124 is expected: QEMU was stopped by the 20 s time limit after the boot ROM gave up
hardware:  emulated NIC (QEMU e1000 model) on QEMU's user-mode network; no physical NIC, PHY or cable involved
